/T (Step segmentation is a source of bias. Breaking a continuous CoT into discrete reasoning steps requires a heuristic \(e.g., paragraph splits\). Poor segmentation produces misaligned targets, which can bias the predictor toward learning artifacts of the splitting strategy rather than genuine logical transitions.)
/E (Step segmentation is a source of bias. Breaking a continuous CoT into discrete reasoning steps requires a heuristic \(e.g., paragraph splits\). Poor segmentation produces misaligned targets, which can bias the predictor toward learning artifacts of the splitting strategy rather than genuine logical transitions.)
/Pg 21 0 R
